22:07.426 --> 22:10.884
KATE: He was left at home
by accident last year.

22:10.929 --> 22:13.159
PETER: Yeah,
that's what my wife meant...

22:13.198 --> 22:16.224
when she said
it's a family travel tradition.

22:18.804 --> 22:22.296
We'll call Chicago and, uh...
notify them of the situation.

22:22.374 --> 22:25.172
The odds are that's where he is.

22:26.111 --> 22:27.237
PETER: Thanks.

22:27.279 --> 22:30.339
It's very unlikely
he'd be anywhere else.

22:43.795 --> 22:45.285
[Honk honk]

22:45.330 --> 22:46.922
TRUCK DRlVER: Watch out, kid!

22:59.745 --> 23:01.679
MAN: Yo, where's your manifest?

23:07.185 --> 23:08.311
HARRY: Here we are, Marv.

23:08.353 --> 23:11.345
New York City,
the land of opportunity.

23:12.457 --> 23:13.617
Smell that?

23:14.526 --> 23:15.652
MARV: Yeah.

23:15.694 --> 23:17.457
You know what that is?

23:17.496 --> 23:18.656
Fish.

23:18.697 --> 23:19.789
It's freedom.

23:19.831 --> 23:21.594
No, it's fish.

23:21.633 --> 23:24.625
It's freedom, and it's money.

23:24.669 --> 23:26.136
OK, OK. It's freedom.

23:26.171 --> 23:28.571
Let's get out of here
before somebody sees us.

23:29.508 --> 23:30.668
And it's fish.

23:37.149 --> 23:39.515
HARRY: Yup, one quick score.

23:39.551 --> 23:42.349
We get ourselves a couple
of phony passports...

23:42.387 --> 23:44.912
we hightail it
to some foreign country.

23:45.957 --> 23:47.117
MARV: Arizona?

23:52.364 --> 23:54.764
That's very smart, Marv.

23:54.800 --> 23:57.894
You bust out of jail to rob
fourteen cents from Santa Claus?

23:57.969 --> 23:59.436
Every little bit helps.

23:59.471 --> 24:02.463
Besides,
now we got our new nickname.

24:02.541 --> 24:04.600
We're the Sticky Bandits.

24:05.510 --> 24:07.569
Real cute.

24:07.612 --> 24:08.909
-Very cute.
-Huh?

24:25.363 --> 24:26.830
KEVlN: The Plaza Hotel...

24:26.865 --> 24:29.629
New York's most exciting
hotel experience.

24:42.481 --> 24:44.176
Sick.

25:41.773 --> 25:43.604
MARV: What's the matter?

25:43.642 --> 25:45.166
HARRY: Thought I saw something.

25:54.586 --> 25:56.713
Pardonnez-moi, mon cherie.

25:58.623 --> 26:00.022
WOMAN: Hmm.

26:01.159 --> 26:02.854
HARRY: Serves you right.
Come on, let's go!

26:03.895 --> 26:05.123
MARV: I think she likes me.

26:06.831 --> 26:08.560
Ahh.

26:43.001 --> 26:44.434
Excuse me. Where's the lobby?

26:44.502 --> 26:46.094
Down the hall and to the left.

26:46.171 --> 26:47.536
Thanks.

27:01.119 --> 27:02.780
Wow!

27:11.329 --> 27:13.923
TAPE: Guests of The New
Celebrity Ding Dang Dong...

27:13.965 --> 27:16.832
stay at the world-renowned
Plaza Hotel...

27:16.901 --> 27:19.392
New York's most exciting
hotel experience.

27:19.471 --> 27:25.706
For reservations call
toll-free 1-800-759-3000.

27:26.978 --> 27:28.468
I'll do just that.

27:29.814 --> 27:32.749
KEVlN: Howdy-do. This is
Peter McCallister, the father.

27:32.784 --> 27:34.376
I'd like a hotel room, please...

27:34.419 --> 27:37.354
with an extra-large bed, a TV...

27:37.389 --> 27:38.754
and one of those
little refrigerators...

27:38.790 --> 27:40.417
you have to open with a key.

27:41.059 --> 27:43.027
Credit card? You got it.

27:46.698 --> 27:49.258
Plaza hotel reservations.
May I help you?

27:49.300 --> 27:50.460
RECORDlNG: [Slow speed]
Howdy-do.

27:50.535 --> 27:53.595
This is Peter McCallister,
the father.

27:53.672 --> 27:56.072
I'd like a hotel room, please...

27:56.107 --> 27:58.974
with an extra-large bed, a TV...

27:59.010 --> 28:01.205
and one of those
little refrigerators...

28:01.246 --> 28:03.214
you have to open with a key.

28:03.248 --> 28:05.910
Sir, you'll need a major
credit card upon check-in.

28:05.950 --> 28:08.851
RECORDlNG:
Credit card? You got it.

28:09.487 --> 28:11.216
WOMAN:
Thank you. Enjoy your stay.

28:15.060 --> 28:18.120
CONClERGE: Yes, two at 8:00,
Henri--Mr. Yamamoto.

28:19.197 --> 28:20.357
Hold on a second.

28:25.070 --> 28:26.469
I'll call you back, Henri.

28:29.007 --> 28:30.133
Hi.

28:35.046 --> 28:36.536
Can I help you?

28:36.581 --> 28:38.640
Reservation for McCallister?

28:40.552 --> 28:42.782
A reservation for yourself?

28:42.821 --> 28:45.517
Ma'am, my feet are hardly
touching the ground.

28:45.557 --> 28:47.457
I'm barely able
to look over this counter.

28:47.492 --> 28:50.222
How could I make
a hotel reservation?

28:50.261 --> 28:51.455
Think about it--

28:51.496 --> 28:54.488
a kid going into a hotel,
making a reservation?

28:54.532 --> 28:56.625
I don't think so.

28:57.969 --> 28:59.800
I'm confused.

28:59.838 --> 29:01.362
I'm traveling with my dad.

29:01.439 --> 29:03.737
He's on business.
He's at a meeting.

29:03.775 --> 29:05.072
I hate meetings...

29:05.110 --> 29:06.873
plus I'm not allowed to go in.

29:06.911 --> 29:08.276
I can only sit in the lobby.

29:08.313 --> 29:09.439
That's boring...

29:09.481 --> 29:11.472
so my dad dropped me off here.

29:12.684 --> 29:13.810
He gave me his credit card...

29:13.852 --> 29:15.820
and said whoever
was checking people in...

29:15.854 --> 29:17.378
to let me in the hotel room...

29:17.422 --> 29:19.481
so I won't get into mischief...

29:19.524 --> 29:21.992
and, ma'am, sometimes I do
get into mischief.

29:23.194 --> 29:25.389
We all do!

29:27.699 --> 29:29.030
OFFlCER: Merry Christmas.

29:31.035 --> 29:32.332
No sign of him.

29:32.403 --> 29:34.928
We'll have to be able
to get ahold of you.

29:35.006 --> 29:37.304
-You have hotel arrangements?
-Yeah.

29:37.342 --> 29:40.038
Do you have
a recent photo of the boy?

29:41.913 --> 29:43.312
PETER: I have one in my wallet.

29:44.749 --> 29:46.307
I don't have my wallet.

29:47.852 --> 29:50.218
My wallet's in my bag.

29:50.255 --> 29:51.882
Kevin was looking in my bag
at the airport.

29:51.923 --> 29:54.016
He was looking for batteries.
Kevin has my wallet.

29:54.058 --> 29:55.923
Did you have credit cards
in the wallet?

29:55.960 --> 29:57.359
Credit cards, money.

29:57.395 --> 29:59.955
We'll notify
the credit card companies.

29:59.998 --> 30:01.124
If your son has the cards...

30:01.166 --> 30:04.693
we can get a location on him
when and if he uses them.

30:04.769 --> 30:07.863
I don't think Kevin even knows
how to use a credit card.

30:10.642 --> 30:11.904
Wow! It worked.

30:16.047 --> 30:18.140
-Cedric.
-Yes?

30:18.183 --> 30:20.549
Don't count your tips
in public...

30:21.853 --> 30:25.949
and find out everything you can
about that young fellow.

30:26.624 --> 30:27.784
WOMAN: Front, please.

30:33.097 --> 30:35.691
Enjoy your stay with us.

30:35.767 --> 30:38.861
Don't forget to remind your dad
when he arrives...

30:38.937 --> 30:41.428
that he has to come down
and sign a couple of things.

30:41.506 --> 30:43.872
KEVlN: Thank you.
You've been most helpful.

30:43.908 --> 30:45.432
CEDRlC:
May I take your bag, sir?

30:48.513 --> 30:49.707
[Elevator bell rings]

30:49.747 --> 30:51.146
CEDRlC: Up here to your left.

30:52.283 --> 30:55.218
You know, Herbert Hoover
once stayed here on this floor.

30:55.253 --> 30:56.720
KEVlN: The vacuum guy?

30:56.754 --> 30:58.381
CEDRlC: No, the, uh, president.

31:03.962 --> 31:06.362
This is one of our
finest suites, sir.

31:14.606 --> 31:16.301
This is great!

31:21.512 --> 31:24.948
KEVlN:
Wow! A huge bed just for me!

31:31.856 --> 31:32.982
Luxurious...

31:33.024 --> 31:34.423
and spacious.

31:41.032 --> 31:42.693
How convenient!

31:45.703 --> 31:46.863
Hey!

31:49.841 --> 31:51.274
Did you want me
to put the key in the bag...

31:52.176 --> 31:53.609
or did you just want
to hang on to it?

31:53.645 --> 31:55.237
I'll hang on to it.

31:58.650 --> 32:00.345
Is everything all right, sir?

32:00.385 --> 32:01.647
Is the temperature
in the room OK?

32:01.686 --> 32:02.812
It's OK.

32:02.854 --> 32:04.378
Do you know how the TV works?

32:04.422 --> 32:06.913
I'm ten years old. TV's my life.

32:07.926 --> 32:09.086
Well...

32:13.231 --> 32:14.357
Oh, I'm sorry.

32:19.604 --> 32:21.799
And there's plenty more
where that came from.

32:24.709 --> 32:25.869
CEDRlC: Thank you.

32:31.449 --> 32:33.474
BOBBY HELMS SlNGlNG:
Jingle bell, jingle bell

32:33.518 --> 32:35.247
Jingle bell rock

32:35.286 --> 32:39.188
Jingle bells swing
and jingle bells ring

32:39.223 --> 32:43.489
Snowin' and blowin' up
bushels of fun

32:43.528 --> 32:47.430
Nowthe jingle hop has begun

32:47.465 --> 32:50.696
Giddyap, jingle horse,
pick up yourfeet

32:51.536 --> 32:53.595
Jingle around the clock

32:53.638 --> 32:56.232
Would it bother anyone
if I worked on my cannonballs?

32:56.274 --> 32:58.003
MAN ON LEFT: No.

32:58.042 --> 32:59.566
Thanks.

32:59.610 --> 33:01.805
BOBBY HELMS SlNGlNG:
That's the jingle bell

33:01.846 --> 33:03.780
That's the jingle bell

33:03.815 --> 33:09.412
That's the jingle bell rock

33:13.191 --> 33:14.351
KEVlN: Yikes!

33:36.180 --> 33:38.546
This is a vacation.

33:39.417 --> 33:41.009
Hold it right there.

33:41.753 --> 33:43.448
It's me, Johnny.

33:43.488 --> 33:45.456
I knew it was you.

33:45.490 --> 33:48.118
I could smell you
getting off the elevator.

33:49.027 --> 33:50.187
Two scoops, sir?

33:50.862 --> 33:53.296
Two? Make it three.
I'm not driving.

33:53.331 --> 33:56.232
WOMAN ON TV:
It's gardenias, Johnny...

33:56.267 --> 33:57.564
your favorite.

33:57.602 --> 34:00.230
You was here last night, too,
wasn't you?

34:01.072 --> 34:03.336
I was singin'
at the Blue Monkey last night.

34:03.374 --> 34:05.968
She was not! She was smooching
with your brother.

34:06.010 --> 34:08.069
You was here...

34:08.112 --> 34:09.977
and you was smooching
with my brother!

34:10.014 --> 34:11.879
WOMAN ON TV: That's
a dirty, rotten lie, Johnny.

34:11.916 --> 34:13.042
Don't give me that.

34:13.084 --> 34:14.949
You been smooching
with everybody!

34:14.986 --> 34:17.716
Snuffy, Al, Leo...

34:17.755 --> 34:19.848
Iittle Mo with the gimpy leg...

34:19.891 --> 34:22.325
Cheeks, Bony Bob, Cliff.

34:22.360 --> 34:24.521
I could go on forever, baby.

34:24.595 --> 34:26.256
WOMAN ON TV:
You got me all wrong.

34:26.330 --> 34:27.422
JOHNNY: All right.

34:27.498 --> 34:29.056
I believe you...

34:29.133 --> 34:31.499
but my Tommy gun don't!

34:31.536 --> 34:32.764
Johnny!

34:33.838 --> 34:35.703
You're the only duck in my pond!

34:35.740 --> 34:38.607
Get down on your knees
and tell me you love me.

34:38.643 --> 34:41.612
WOMAN ON TV: Baby!
I'm over the moon for ya!

34:41.646 --> 34:43.671
You got to do betterthan that!

34:44.415 --> 34:46.178
If my love was an ocean...

34:46.217 --> 34:49.448
Lindy'd have to take
two airplanes to get across it!

34:50.888 --> 34:53.857
Maybe I'm off my hinges,
but I believe you.

34:53.891 --> 34:56.689
-Oh!
-That's why I'll let you go.

34:56.761 --> 34:59.730
I'm going to give you
to the count of three...

34:59.764 --> 35:03.825
to get your lousy,
lying, lowdown...

35:03.901 --> 35:06.631
four-flushing carcass
out my door!

35:06.671 --> 35:08.730
She's rat bait.

35:08.773 --> 35:09.967
One...

35:11.008 --> 35:12.168
two...

35:14.512 --> 35:16.776
Ha ha ha ha ha!

35:20.718 --> 35:22.049
Three!

35:22.820 --> 35:25.653
Merry Christmas,
you filthy animal...

35:27.458 --> 35:29.016
and a happy New Year.

35:29.927 --> 35:31.053
[Gunshot]

35:41.906 --> 35:43.237
[Elevator bell rings]

36:02.560 --> 36:03.686
[German accent]
Housekeeping.

36:03.761 --> 36:04.853
[Gasps]

36:04.929 --> 36:06.829
ALAN JACKSON SlNGlNG:
Have a holly, jolly Christmas

36:36.394 --> 36:38.123
[Shower running]

36:44.635 --> 36:45.761
TAPE OF FRANK SlNGlNG:
We know a guy

36:45.803 --> 36:48.397
Who can really do the cool jerk

36:50.074 --> 36:51.405
We know a guy

36:51.442 --> 36:54.570
Who can really do the cool jerk

36:54.612 --> 36:58.605
Well, this cat
they're talkin' about

36:58.649 --> 37:01.140
I wonder who could it be

37:01.185 --> 37:04.416
'Cause I know
I'm the heaviest cat

37:04.455 --> 37:07.583
The heaviest cat
you ever did see

37:07.625 --> 37:10.389
Women see me
walkin' down the street

37:10.428 --> 37:13.363
None of the fellas want to speak

37:13.397 --> 37:15.661
On their faces,
they wear a silly smirk

37:15.700 --> 37:21.138
'Cause they know I'm the king
of the cool jerk

37:21.172 --> 37:22.434
Whoo, cool jerk

37:24.942 --> 37:26.842
Get out of here,
you nosy little pervert...

37:26.877 --> 37:28.367
or I'm going to slap you silly!

37:31.115 --> 37:32.241
Oh, oh, oh...

37:32.283 --> 37:34.911
you're cooking, Frankie!

37:34.952 --> 37:36.249
CONClERGE: Oh!

37:49.667 --> 37:53.159
ANDY WlLLlAMS SlNGlNG:
It's the most wonderful time

37:53.237 --> 37:55.501
Of the year

37:55.539 --> 37:56.699
BACKGROUND SlNGERS: Ding dong

37:56.741 --> 37:58.538
ANDYWlLLlAMS:
With the kids jingle-belling

37:58.576 --> 38:00.510
And everyone telling you

38:00.544 --> 38:03.411
Be of good cheer

38:03.447 --> 38:08.009
It's the most wonderful time
of the year

38:08.052 --> 38:11.385
BACKGROUND SlNGERS:
Ding dong, ding dong

38:11.422 --> 38:13.549
FRANK: Didn't look this bad
on our honeymoon.

38:30.941 --> 38:32.704
KEVlN:
Hey! Uncle Rob lives here.

38:32.743 --> 38:35.712
If they're back from Paris,
I'll drop in on them.

38:36.447 --> 38:38.574
They usually give
pretty good presents.

39:25.663 --> 39:32.592
CHlLDREN SlNGlNG: Distant stars
at home up in the heavens

39:32.670 --> 39:36.663
What a sight to see

39:36.707 --> 39:38.504
Are they there to guide me?

39:38.542 --> 39:40.100
KEVlN: Good night, Mom.

39:40.144 --> 39:44.137
CHlLDREN SlNGlNG:
Starlight shine bright

39:44.181 --> 39:45.648
See me through the dark night

39:45.683 --> 39:46.843
KATE: Good night, Kevin.

39:47.885 --> 39:51.651
CHlLDREN SlNGlNG:
Guide my pathway

39:51.689 --> 39:52.849
Guide me home for Christmas day

40:14.345 --> 40:16.040
Your drawers, sir.

40:16.080 --> 40:18.878
Jeez! Don't flash
these babies around here!

40:18.916 --> 40:21.077
There could be girls
on this floor!

40:21.118 --> 40:22.983
I was very careful, sir.

40:23.020 --> 40:25.955
You can't be too careful
when it involves underwear.

40:25.990 --> 40:27.355
I understand.

40:28.058 --> 40:30.424
I'm sorry. You wanted a tip.

40:30.494 --> 40:32.462
That won't be necessary, sir.

40:32.496 --> 40:35.056
I still have some tip left over.

40:36.700 --> 40:38.895
No tip? OK.

40:40.604 --> 40:42.868
No, no, no! Wait, wait, wait!

40:43.007 --> 40:44.167
[Elevator bell rings]

40:44.208 --> 40:45.869
MAN:
How do I get to Columbus Circle?

40:45.910 --> 40:48.140
CONClERGE: The doorman will be
happy to find you a taxi as--

40:49.113 --> 40:50.307
Mr. McCallister!

40:53.684 --> 40:55.015
Uh...excuse me.

40:55.052 --> 40:56.212
MAN: Sure.

40:59.623 --> 41:01.557
And how are we this morning?

41:01.592 --> 41:03.389
Fine.
Is my transportation here?

41:03.427 --> 41:05.156
Out in front, sir.

41:05.229 --> 41:07.891
A limousine and a pizza...

41:07.965 --> 41:09.557
compliments of the Plaza Hotel.

41:10.234 --> 41:12.293
I do hope your father
understands...

41:12.369 --> 41:14.837
that last night I was simply
checking the room...

41:14.872 --> 41:16.931
to make sure
everything was in order.

41:16.974 --> 41:18.737
Oh, he was pretty mad.

41:18.776 --> 41:20.038
He was?

41:20.077 --> 41:21.305
He said he didn't come
to New York...

41:21.345 --> 41:23.711
to get his naked rear end
spied on.

41:24.381 --> 41:26.110
Of course not.

41:26.150 --> 41:28.118
Will he be down...soon?

41:28.152 --> 41:29.585
He already left.

41:31.388 --> 41:33.253
Oh. I would have liked...

41:33.290 --> 41:35.485
to have offered
my personal apology.

41:35.526 --> 41:37.357
If some guy looked at you
in the shower...

41:37.428 --> 41:39.089
would you ever want
to see him again?

41:39.897 --> 41:41.364
I suppose not.

41:41.432 --> 41:43.696
I don't think you'll see him
for the rest of our trip.

41:44.535 --> 41:45.695
I understand.

41:46.537 --> 41:47.697
Bye.

41:51.075 --> 41:52.508
Have a lovely day.

41:59.383 --> 42:01.374
"M, M, M...

42:01.418 --> 42:04.216
"McCallister."

42:17.134 --> 42:19.034
-Morning, Mr. McCallister.
-Good morning.

42:23.807 --> 42:25.968
JOHNNY MATHlS SlNGlNG:
It's beginning to look a lot

42:26.010 --> 42:27.170
Iike Christmas

42:27.211 --> 42:30.442
CEDRlC: Mr. McCallister,
here's your very own...

42:30.481 --> 42:32.142
cheese pizza.

42:32.182 --> 42:35.151
JOHNNY MATHlS SlNGlNG:
Take a look in the five and ten

42:35.185 --> 42:36.846
Listening once again

42:36.887 --> 42:41.017
With candy canes
and silver lanes aglow

42:41.058 --> 42:45.620
It's beginning to look a lot
like Christmas

42:45.696 --> 42:49.723
Toys in every store

42:49.800 --> 42:51.791
But the prettiest sight to see

42:51.869 --> 42:53.427
Is the holly that will be

42:53.504 --> 42:54.630
KEVlN: Hello?

42:54.672 --> 42:56.299
DRlVER: Hello.

42:56.340 --> 42:57.932
Know any good toy stores?

42:57.975 --> 42:59.442
Yes, sir!

43:03.080 --> 43:05.014
BACKGROUND SlNGERS:
It's beginning to look a lot

43:05.049 --> 43:07.347
Iike Christmas

43:07.384 --> 43:11.650
Soon the bells will start

43:11.689 --> 43:14.021
JOHNNY MATHlS: And the thing
that will make them ring

43:14.058 --> 43:15.923
Is the carol that you sing

43:15.960 --> 43:17.791
Right within your heart

43:17.861 --> 43:19.055
CONClERGE: Bingo!

43:34.211 --> 43:37.703
HARRY: Get out of here!
Go on! Get out of here!

43:37.781 --> 43:40.147
Beat it! Get out of here!

43:40.184 --> 43:41.617
Hey...Marv!

43:41.652 --> 43:43.586
Get over here!
I got to talk to you!

43:54.131 --> 43:55.359
MARV: Whoa! Whoa!

43:57.901 --> 43:59.027
Would you like a scarf?

43:59.069 --> 44:01.833
Forget the scarf, Marv.
We got to talk.

44:03.173 --> 44:05.232
We don't have the equipment
to pull off anything big--

44:05.275 --> 44:07.402
you know, your banks,
jewelry stores.

44:07.444 --> 44:09.036
We don't want goods.

44:09.113 --> 44:12.082
We need cash,
and we need it now.

44:12.116 --> 44:13.583
MARV: How about, uh...

44:13.617 --> 44:15.084
hotels?

44:15.119 --> 44:16.814
Tourists carry lots of cash.

44:16.854 --> 44:18.321
There's no guarantees.

44:18.355 --> 44:19.652
I got a better idea.

44:19.723 --> 44:21.953
Stores don't deposit cash
on Christmas Eve.

44:21.992 --> 44:24.426
The only stores
that'll have cash on hand...

44:24.461 --> 44:27.555
are ones that deal
in moderate-priced goods.

44:27.598 --> 44:29.031
MARV: Right...right.

44:29.066 --> 44:32.593
HARRY: What stores make
lots of cash Christmas Eve...

44:32.636 --> 44:34.866
that nobody's going to think
to rob?

44:35.639 --> 44:36.833
Candy stores.

44:38.075 --> 44:40.100
Nine-year-olds
rob candy stores, Marv.

44:41.045 --> 44:43.240
This is what I had in mind.

44:44.915 --> 44:46.007
MARV: That's brilliant, Harry.

44:46.083 --> 44:47.448
Brilliant!

44:49.153 --> 44:51.280
HARRY: Yep.
There's nobody dumb enough...

44:51.321 --> 44:54.017
to knock off a toy store
on Christmas Eve.

44:54.058 --> 44:55.616
Oh, yes, there is.

45:14.044 --> 45:15.136
DRlVER: Here we are, sir...

45:15.212 --> 45:17.146
Duncan's Toy Chest.

45:18.415 --> 45:20.474
Merry Christmas, Kevin.

46:03.327 --> 46:06.353
This is the greatest accident
of my life.

46:24.648 --> 46:26.775
Marv. Marv!

46:26.850 --> 46:29.478
Hey, nice house,
but there's no bathroom in it.

46:32.556 --> 46:33.853
MARV: What's the plan?

46:33.891 --> 46:36.826
HARRY: Everybody leaves
for a nice holiday off.

46:36.860 --> 46:38.259
We come out
of our little houses...

46:41.765 --> 46:43.426
Yeah, then what?

46:43.467 --> 46:45.833
We empty the registers and
walk out like we own the joint.

46:45.869 --> 46:47.564
Great plan, Harry!

46:48.939 --> 46:50.065
MAN: Shake his hand.

46:50.107 --> 46:52.735
CASHlER: Well, now thank you
and merry Christmas.

46:52.776 --> 46:54.107
Say hello to the family.

46:55.579 --> 46:57.911
Oh, yes. Let me see.

46:57.948 --> 46:59.472
Eh...

47:00.751 --> 47:02.480
You shopping alone?

47:02.519 --> 47:03.986
In New York?

47:04.021 --> 47:05.955
Sir, I'm afraid
of my own shadow.

47:05.989 --> 47:07.889
CASHlER: I was just checking.

47:07.925 --> 47:09.415
KEVlN:
That's very responsible of you.

47:09.459 --> 47:11.086
CASHlER: Oh, well, thank you.

47:11.128 --> 47:13.028
KEVlN: My pleasure.

47:13.063 --> 47:16.794
CASHlER: That'll be $23.75.

47:18.602 --> 47:19.728
My, my, my!

47:19.770 --> 47:21.761
Where did you get
all that money?

47:22.906 --> 47:24.897
Uh...I have a lot
of grandmothers.

47:24.942 --> 47:26.068
CASHlER: Oh.

47:26.109 --> 47:28.134
Well, that explains it.

47:30.314 --> 47:32.043
This is a really nice store--

47:32.115 --> 47:35.084
one of the finer toy dealerships
I've ever visited.

47:35.118 --> 47:36.449
CASHlER: Oh, well, thank you.

47:36.486 --> 47:38.454
KEVlN: Mr. Duncan
must be a pretty nice guy...

47:38.522 --> 47:40.490
Ietting all the kids
come into his store...

47:40.524 --> 47:41.991
and play with his toys.

47:42.025 --> 47:43.925
Most toy stores prohibit that.

47:43.961 --> 47:45.485
-Oh, is that so?
-Yep.

47:45.529 --> 47:47.929
Well, he loves kids.

47:47.965 --> 47:49.432
As a matter of fact...

47:49.466 --> 47:51.934
all the money
the store takes in today...

47:51.969 --> 47:55.598
Mr. Duncan is donating it
to the Children's Hospital...

47:55.639 --> 47:57.937
and the day after Christmas...

47:57.975 --> 48:01.138
we empty all the money
in the cash register...

48:01.211 --> 48:04.669
and Mr. Duncan just takes it
right down to the hospital.

48:04.748 --> 48:06.340
That's very generous of him.

48:06.416 --> 48:10.113
Well, children
bring him a lot of joy...

48:10.153 --> 48:13.452
as they do to everyone
who appreciates them.

48:18.996 --> 48:20.623
I'm not supposed to spend
this money...

48:20.664 --> 48:22.723
but I have twenty dollars
from shoveling snow...

48:22.766 --> 48:24.063
in a jar in our garage...

48:24.101 --> 48:26.035
where my older brother
can't find it.

48:26.069 --> 48:28.196
So I'll pay my mother back
with that.

48:28.238 --> 48:30.206
You can give this
to Mr. Duncan.

48:30.240 --> 48:32.504
The hospital
needs it more than I do.

48:32.542 --> 48:34.533
Besides, I'll probably
spend it on stuff...

48:34.578 --> 48:37.308
that'll rot my teeth
and my mind.

48:37.381 --> 48:43.047
Aw...that's--
that's very sweet of you.

48:43.086 --> 48:46.419
Eh...you see that tree there?

48:46.456 --> 48:50.324
To show our appreciation
for your generosity...

48:50.360 --> 48:53.227
I'm going to let you select
an object from that tree...

48:53.263 --> 48:55.231
that you can take home with you.

48:55.265 --> 48:57.233
-Free?
-Oh, yeah.

48:57.267 --> 48:59.497
CASHlER: Eh...may--
may I make a suggestion?

48:59.536 --> 49:00.662
KEVlN: OK.

49:00.704 --> 49:03.002
CASHlER: Take the turtledoves.

49:03.040 --> 49:04.940
I could have two?

49:04.975 --> 49:07.535
Well, two turtledoves.

49:07.611 --> 49:08.805
I'll tell you what you do.

49:09.880 --> 49:11.745
You keep one...

49:11.782 --> 49:15.616
and you give the other one
to a very special person.

49:15.652 --> 49:17.085
You see...

49:17.120 --> 49:21.113
turtledoves are a symbol
of friendship and love.

49:21.959 --> 49:25.554
As long as each of you
have your turtledove...

49:25.595 --> 49:28.189
you'll be friends forever.

49:28.231 --> 49:30.699
Wow! I never knew that.

49:30.734 --> 49:32.599
I thought they were
just part of a song.

49:32.636 --> 49:33.864
They are...

49:33.904 --> 49:36.600
and--and for that
very special reason.

49:36.640 --> 49:38.403
Wow!

49:38.442 --> 49:40.137
Thanks.

49:40.177 --> 49:41.474
Merry Christmas.

49:41.545 --> 49:43.877
Merry Christmas to you, too.

49:43.914 --> 49:45.472
Be sure to bundle up
if you go outside.

49:45.549 --> 49:46.811
It's a little nippy.

49:46.850 --> 49:50.183
Oh, thank you, l--I'll do that.

50:27.057 --> 50:29.184
Well, where to?

50:29.226 --> 50:32.093
You promised you'd take me
to the Central Park Zoo.

50:40.170 --> 50:41.603
Hey!

50:41.638 --> 50:43.128
Look who it is, Marv.

50:46.576 --> 50:48.476
Come on. Let's get him.

50:49.980 --> 50:52.175
WOMAN: Oh! Hey!

50:54.251 --> 50:55.548
HARRY: Hiya, pal.

50:55.585 --> 50:56.745
[Kevin gasps]

51:03.427 --> 51:09.229
Aah!

51:09.266 --> 51:10.631
Aah!

51:14.504 --> 51:15.766
HARRY: Come on!

51:31.054 --> 51:32.214
MAN: Hey!

51:38.061 --> 51:39.426
MAN: Hey! Watch it, man!

51:39.463 --> 51:41.897
[Package shatters]

51:41.932 --> 51:44.264
VENDOR: Buy now and avoid
the Christmas rush.

51:44.301 --> 51:47.270
Two forfive dollars,
fourforten.

51:47.304 --> 51:48.430
All right.

51:48.472 --> 51:50.030
MARV: There he is!

51:50.073 --> 51:51.665
VENDOR: All right, kiddo!

51:51.708 --> 51:53.676
-Thanks.
-Merry Christmas.

51:53.710 --> 51:55.701
-Oh! Hey!
-Whoa!

51:55.745 --> 51:57.542
MAN: Excuse me!

52:23.473 --> 52:24.906
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

52:24.941 --> 52:26.135
-Oh!
-Oh!

52:28.211 --> 52:29.576
MARV: Ohh!

52:30.914 --> 52:32.814
Yes!

52:32.849 --> 52:34.180
WOMAN:
Thank you for your suggestion.

52:34.217 --> 52:36.378
CONClERGE:
My duty and my pleasure.

52:47.564 --> 52:50.431
KEVlN: You got to help me!
There's two guys after me!

52:50.467 --> 52:52.332
What's the matter?

52:52.369 --> 52:54.098
Store wouldn't take your...

52:54.938 --> 52:57.168
stolen credit card?

52:58.041 --> 53:01.033
Let's see what the police
have to say about this.

53:06.283 --> 53:07.409
HARRY: Get up! Get up!

53:09.753 --> 53:11.118
Come on! Let's go get him!

53:13.490 --> 53:16.288
CONClERGE:
Get back here, you little thief!

53:18.995 --> 53:20.292
Stop that child!

53:23.266 --> 53:24.426
CEDRlC: Grab him!

53:29.139 --> 53:30.504
[Elevator bell rings]

53:40.083 --> 53:42.517
CONClERGE: You little sh--

53:44.087 --> 53:46.385
I've committed
credit card fraud.

53:46.423 --> 53:48.687
CONClERGE: Get me security!

53:48.725 --> 53:52.058
We've got to stop
that delinquent!

53:52.095 --> 53:54.359
Come along, Cedric.

54:12.983 --> 54:14.951
I've had enough
of this vacation.

54:14.985 --> 54:16.612
I'm going home.

54:27.130 --> 54:28.859
Hold it right there.

54:31.101 --> 54:32.762
This is the concierge, sir!

54:33.637 --> 54:35.867
I knew it was you.

54:35.905 --> 54:38.100
I could smell you
getting off the elevator.

54:40.310 --> 54:43.006
You was here last night, too,
wasn't you?

54:45.048 --> 54:48.449
Yes, sir...I was.

54:48.485 --> 54:49.952
JOHNNY: You was here...

54:50.020 --> 54:52.352
and you was smooching
with my brother!

54:54.658 --> 54:57.752
I'm--I'm afraid
you're mistaken, sir.

54:57.794 --> 54:59.284
Don't give me that.

54:59.329 --> 55:01.320
You been smooching
with everybody!

55:01.364 --> 55:04.231
Snuffy, Al, Leo...

55:04.267 --> 55:06.030
Iittle Mo with the gimpy leg...

55:06.069 --> 55:08.469
Cheeks, Bony Bob, Cliff.

55:08.505 --> 55:10.029
[Gasps]

55:12.242 --> 55:13.402
No!

55:15.011 --> 55:16.603
It's a lie!

55:16.680 --> 55:18.614
JOHNNY:
I could go on forever, baby.

55:19.582 --> 55:21.447
I'm terribly sorry, sir...

55:21.484 --> 55:24.078
but I'm afraid
you're mistaken.

55:24.120 --> 55:26.111
We're looking for a young man.

55:26.156 --> 55:27.646
All right.

55:27.691 --> 55:29.352
I believe you...

55:29.392 --> 55:30.825
but my Tommy gun don't!

55:32.195 --> 55:35.028
Get down on your knees
and tell me you love me.

55:37.701 --> 55:39.259
CONClERGE: On your knees.

55:48.311 --> 55:51.007
I love you!

55:54.351 --> 55:56.216
You got to do betterthan that!

55:57.721 --> 55:59.951
EVERYONE: I love you!

56:01.691 --> 56:04.888
JOHNNY: Maybe I'm off my hinges,
but I believe you.

56:04.928 --> 56:07.021
That's why
I'm going to let you go.

56:08.098 --> 56:10.760
I'm going to give you
to the count of three...

56:10.800 --> 56:14.930
to get your lousy,
lying, lowdown...

56:14.971 --> 56:17.599
four-flushing carcass
out my door!

56:19.476 --> 56:20.875
-One.
-Open up the door!

56:20.910 --> 56:22.070
Two.

56:24.514 --> 56:26.675
Ha ha ha ha ha!

56:26.750 --> 56:28.217
Ha ha ha ha ha!

56:28.251 --> 56:29.650
[Tommy gun firing]

56:36.359 --> 56:38.088
Three!

56:38.128 --> 56:40.858
JOHNNY: Merry Christmas,
you filthy animal...

56:41.898 --> 56:43.695
[Tommy gun fires]

56:43.733 --> 56:45.826
JOHNNY: and a happy New Year.

56:45.869 --> 56:47.166
[Gunshot]

56:48.505 --> 56:49.631
Stay in your rooms!

56:49.672 --> 56:51.469
This is an emergency!

56:51.508 --> 56:54.841
There's an insane guest
with a gun!

57:05.622 --> 57:10.286
KEVlN: Nooo!

57:10.326 --> 57:11.486
HARRY: Come to papa!

57:14.130 --> 57:16.121
MARV: Ha! Round trip to Miami.

57:16.166 --> 57:18.361
What's the matter?
Get on the wrong plane, squirt?

57:18.401 --> 57:20.369
HARRY: Looks like
you won't be needing this, kid.

57:20.403 --> 57:23.133
MARV: American don't fly to
the promised land, little buddy.

57:23.173 --> 57:24.834
HARRY: Come on!

57:26.443 --> 57:27.876
HARRY:
We spent nine months in jail...

57:27.911 --> 57:30.345
thinking we had
the worst luck in the universe.

57:30.380 --> 57:32.348
We were wrong, little buddy.

57:32.382 --> 57:34.850
MARV: We busted out of
the clink, and we're doing fine.

57:34.918 --> 57:36.385
We'll be doing even better...

57:36.419 --> 57:38.387
because we're not
robbing houses anymore.

57:38.421 --> 57:39.786
Now we're robbing toy stores.

57:39.823 --> 57:41.256
At midnight tonight...

57:41.291 --> 57:42.849
we're hitting
Duncan's Toy Chest.

57:42.926 --> 57:45.190
Five floors of cash.

57:45.228 --> 57:47.128
After that, we grab
a couple of phony passports--

57:47.163 --> 57:50.223
HARRY: Marv!
Marv, you want to shut up?

57:50.266 --> 57:51.392
MARV: What's the difference?

57:51.434 --> 57:53.061
He's not going to talk
to anybody...

57:53.102 --> 57:54.899
except maybe a fish.

57:54.938 --> 57:56.371
Or the undertaker.

57:56.406 --> 57:58.374
HARRY: Let's just get him
to the subway tunnel.

57:58.408 --> 58:01.070
I'll feel a lot better
once we get him on ice.

58:03.246 --> 58:05.043
HARRY:
I've got a gun in my pocket.

58:05.081 --> 58:06.207
You open your mouth...

58:06.249 --> 58:08.342
and you'll be spitting gum
out through your forehead.

58:29.405 --> 58:30.633
Well, hello.

58:34.110 --> 58:36.704
-He did it.
-Did what?

58:39.449 --> 58:40.609
Thanks.

58:44.587 --> 58:45.679
HARRY: Get him, will ya!

58:45.755 --> 58:46.847
MARV: He went in the park.

58:46.923 --> 58:48.049
HARRY: What are you doing?

58:48.124 --> 58:49.284
Get up!

59:23.960 --> 59:25.188
MARV: Overthere!

59:30.099 --> 59:31.225
BOY: Quit it!

59:31.267 --> 59:32.825
-Hey!
-Creep!

59:32.869 --> 59:35.064
-Give it!
-What are you doing?

59:35.738 --> 59:37.706
MARV: Hey, Harry, I got him.

59:37.740 --> 59:39.264
HARRY:
Let me see. That ain't him.

59:39.309 --> 59:41.709
Put him down. That ain't him.

59:42.378 --> 59:44.039
We should've shot him
when we had the chance.

59:44.080 --> 59:46.776
I hate pulling a job knowing
that creep is on the loose.

59:46.816 --> 59:49.512
MARV: What can he do?
Kids are helpless.

59:49.586 --> 59:50.746
HARRY: Not this kid.

59:50.820 --> 59:52.651
MARV: This time,
he doesn't have a houseful...

59:52.689 --> 59:55.055
of dangerous goodies
to get us with.

59:55.091 --> 59:57.059
He's in the park. He's alone.

59:57.093 --> 59:59.391
Kids are a-scared of the park.

59:59.429 --> 01:00:01.397
HARRY: Yeah.
Grown men come in the park...

01:00:01.431 --> 01:00:02.557
and don't leave alive.

01:00:02.599 --> 01:00:04.396
MARV: Yeah.

01:00:04.434 --> 01:00:06.095
HARRY: Good luck, little fella.

01:00:16.913 --> 01:00:18.346
KEVlN: I want to go home.

01:00:19.749 --> 01:00:21.216
Mom, where are you?

01:00:25.622 --> 01:00:27.886
[Speaking Spanish]

01:00:49.612 --> 01:00:51.375
[Telephone rings]

01:00:51.414 --> 01:00:52.881
Turn that down.

01:00:54.951 --> 01:00:56.384
-Hello.
-Kate McCallister, please.

01:00:56.419 --> 01:00:58.614
-This is she.
-Ma'am, we found your son.

01:00:58.688 --> 01:01:01.384
-What?
-The police know where Kevin is.

01:01:01.424 --> 01:01:02.891
MAN: He's in New York City.

01:01:02.925 --> 01:01:04.187
He's in New York.

01:01:04.227 --> 01:01:05.785
-New York?
-New York?

01:01:05.828 --> 01:01:08.388
MAN: He checked into the Plaza
with your husband's credit card.

01:01:08.431 --> 01:01:12.128
I'm sure he was scared.
He's not a troublemaker.

01:01:12.168 --> 01:01:14.568
Would you hold just a second?

01:01:14.604 --> 01:01:16.504
He used your credit card
to check into the Plaza Hotel.

01:01:16.539 --> 01:01:18.200
Do they still have him?

01:01:18.241 --> 01:01:19.401
Do they have him?

01:01:19.442 --> 01:01:21.103
MAN:
No, police are still looking.

01:01:21.144 --> 01:01:23.044
Damn it!

01:01:23.079 --> 01:01:25.604
We're on the next flight out.
Thank you.

01:01:25.648 --> 01:01:26.876
We're going to New York.

01:01:26.916 --> 01:01:28.315
-Yes!
-Yes!

01:01:29.452 --> 01:01:31.977
He ran away when they
questioned him about the card.

01:01:32.055 --> 01:01:33.522
He must be so scared.

01:01:33.589 --> 01:01:35.819
Would he go
to my brother's place?

01:01:35.858 --> 01:01:36.984
Aren't they in Paris?

01:01:37.026 --> 01:01:38.516
Maybe there's a housesitter.

01:01:38.594 --> 01:01:40.391
I thought you said
they're renovating.

01:02:13.796 --> 01:02:16.230
[Knock on door]

01:02:20.503 --> 01:02:22.698
Hello!

01:02:22.739 --> 01:02:24.730
Uncle Rob?

01:02:24.774 --> 01:02:25.832
Aunt Georgette?

01:02:25.875 --> 01:02:28.207
Anybody home?

01:02:28.244 --> 01:02:30.075
Hello!

01:02:30.113 --> 01:02:31.808
Anybody home?

01:02:31.848 --> 01:02:35.249
It's me,
your favorite nephew Kevin.

01:02:35.318 --> 01:02:37.309
Uncle Rob!

01:02:37.386 --> 01:02:39.411
Aunt Georgette!

01:03:00.409 --> 01:03:02.400
[Muttering]

01:03:22.698 --> 01:03:24.393
Watch it, kid!

01:03:24.433 --> 01:03:27.425
Ha ha ha ha ha
ha ha ha ha ha ha!

01:03:27.470 --> 01:03:30.462
Ha ha ha ha ha
ha ha ha ha ha ha!

01:03:30.506 --> 01:03:32.497
WOMAN:
Hey, looking for somebody...

01:03:32.542 --> 01:03:34.737
to read you a bedtime story?

01:03:34.777 --> 01:03:37.473
[Laughing]

01:03:40.750 --> 01:03:42.183
Taxi!

01:03:54.897 --> 01:03:57.331
Boy, it's scary out there.

01:03:59.001 --> 01:04:00.400
Ain't much better in here, kid.

01:04:27.864 --> 01:04:30.526
I don't want to ever take
a vacation like this again.

01:05:01.664 --> 01:05:03.222
Where did all you come from?

01:05:03.266 --> 01:05:05.234
I may not have enough
for everybody.

01:05:05.268 --> 01:05:07.259
How hungry are you guys?

01:05:08.804 --> 01:05:10.999
Well, you guys ate all my food.

01:05:26.389 --> 01:05:29.222
Aah!

01:05:34.363 --> 01:05:36.228
Aah!

01:05:36.265 --> 01:05:37.425
Aah!

01:05:38.367 --> 01:05:40.528
Aah!

01:06:10.700 --> 01:06:13.362
Look, I'm sorry
I screamed in yourface.

01:06:13.402 --> 01:06:15.734
You were just trying
to help me, right?

01:06:19.308 --> 01:06:20.570
I'm Kevin McCallister.

01:06:21.744 --> 01:06:23.507
Your birds are real nice.

01:06:24.513 --> 01:06:25.912
I've seen you before.

01:06:25.948 --> 01:06:28.473
You had pigeons all over you.

01:06:28.551 --> 01:06:30.781
At first,
you looked kind of scary.

01:06:30.853 --> 01:06:33.321
But when I think about it,
it's not so bad.

01:06:33.356 --> 01:06:35.449
They must be all over you
'cause they like you.

01:06:37.693 --> 01:06:39.820
If I'm bothering you,
I can leave.

01:06:39.862 --> 01:06:41.727
Am I bothering you?

01:06:42.865 --> 01:06:44.127
No.

01:06:45.167 --> 01:06:47.761
Good.
I'm not a pain in the butt?

01:06:49.872 --> 01:06:51.032
No.

01:06:55.778 --> 01:06:57.336
Will those pigeons
come back on their own...

01:06:57.380 --> 01:06:58.779
or do you have to call them?

01:07:10.159 --> 01:07:11.319
WOMAN: Give me your hand.

01:07:15.398 --> 01:07:16.888
They can hear it.

01:07:34.450 --> 01:07:35.974
This is great.

01:07:40.289 --> 01:07:41.688
It's pretty cold out.

01:07:41.724 --> 01:07:44.192
I could sure go
for a cup of hot chocolate.

01:07:44.260 --> 01:07:46.694
How about you? My treat.

01:07:51.667 --> 01:07:54.397
KEVlN: I'd hate to spend
Christmas Eve in Central Park.

01:07:54.437 --> 01:07:56.803
Can we go someplace warm?

01:07:56.839 --> 01:07:58.932
WOMAN: Yes. I know a place.

01:08:06.048 --> 01:08:10.041
[Playing "Adeste Fideles"]

01:08:46.422 --> 01:08:47.582
KEVlN: Nice music.

01:08:49.258 --> 01:08:51.192
This place is great.

01:08:52.261 --> 01:08:54.752
WOMAN: I've heard the world's
great music from here.

01:08:56.765 --> 01:08:59.256
Ella Fitzgerald, Count Basie...

01:08:59.335 --> 01:09:01.326
Frank Sinatra...

01:09:01.403 --> 01:09:02.802
Luciano Pavarotti.

01:09:08.677 --> 01:09:10.474
So, do you bring your friends
up here?

01:09:12.314 --> 01:09:14.179
I haven't got many friends.

01:09:14.216 --> 01:09:16.616
Oh. Sorry.

01:09:17.253 --> 01:09:18.948
I'm like the birds I care for.

01:09:20.422 --> 01:09:21.753
People pass me in the street.

01:09:21.790 --> 01:09:24.258
They see me,
but they try to ignore me.

01:09:24.293 --> 01:09:26.818
They'd prefer
I wasn't part of their city.

01:09:26.862 --> 01:09:28.193
Yeah.

01:09:28.230 --> 01:09:30.221
It's sorta like that
with my family.

01:09:30.266 --> 01:09:32.234
I'm kinda the pigeon
of the house...

01:09:32.268 --> 01:09:34.133
just because I'm the youngest.

01:09:34.970 --> 01:09:36.494
Everyone fights for position.

01:09:37.439 --> 01:09:39.168
Everybody wants to be seen...

01:09:39.208 --> 01:09:40.334
and heard.

01:09:40.376 --> 01:09:42.139
I guess so.

01:09:42.178 --> 01:09:44.237
I'm seen and heard
pretty much...

01:09:44.280 --> 01:09:46.271
but then I get sent
to my room a lot, too.

01:09:49.285 --> 01:09:51.913
I wasn't always like this,
you know.

01:09:51.954 --> 01:09:53.683
Oh. What were you like before?

01:09:55.057 --> 01:09:56.490
I had a job...

01:09:56.525 --> 01:09:58.152
I had a home...

01:09:58.194 --> 01:09:59.320
I had a family.

01:09:59.361 --> 01:10:00.521
Did you have any kids?

01:10:01.764 --> 01:10:02.924
No.

01:10:04.133 --> 01:10:05.259
Oh, I wanted them...

01:10:06.302 --> 01:10:08.270
but the man I loved...

01:10:08.304 --> 01:10:09.771
fell out of love with me.

01:10:10.639 --> 01:10:12.106
That broke my heart.

01:10:13.008 --> 01:10:15.568
And whenever the chance
to be loved came along again...

01:10:16.712 --> 01:10:18.043
I ran away from it.

01:10:19.248 --> 01:10:20.943
I stopped trusting people.

01:10:20.983 --> 01:10:22.450
No offense...

01:10:22.484 --> 01:10:25.317
but that seems like
sort of a dumb thing to do.

01:10:25.354 --> 01:10:27.879
I was afraid of getting
my heart broken again.

01:10:29.024 --> 01:10:31.185
You see, sometimes
you can trust a person...

01:10:31.227 --> 01:10:33.695
and then,
when things are down...

01:10:33.729 --> 01:10:35.560
they forget about you.

01:10:36.599 --> 01:10:38.328
Maybe they're just too busy.

01:10:38.400 --> 01:10:39.697
Maybe they don't
forget about you...

01:10:39.768 --> 01:10:42.396
but they forget to remember you.

01:10:42.471 --> 01:10:44.234
I don't think people
mean to forget.

01:10:44.273 --> 01:10:46.503
I think it just happens.

01:10:46.542 --> 01:10:49.204
My grandfather says
if my head wasn't screwed on...

01:10:49.245 --> 01:10:50.872
I'd leave it on the school bus.

01:10:50.913 --> 01:10:52.904
I'm just afraid
if I do trust someone...

01:10:52.948 --> 01:10:55.246
I'll get my heart broken again.

01:10:55.284 --> 01:10:56.649
KEVlN: I understand that.

01:10:56.685 --> 01:10:59.620
I used to have a really nice
pair of roller blades.

01:10:59.655 --> 01:11:02.215
I was afraid I'd wreck them...

01:11:02.258 --> 01:11:03.782
so I kept them in the box.

01:11:03.826 --> 01:11:05.919
-You know what happened?
-No.

01:11:05.961 --> 01:11:07.087
I outgrew them.

01:11:07.129 --> 01:11:08.721
I never wore them once
outside...

01:11:08.764 --> 01:11:10.959
just in my room
a couple of times.

01:11:12.501 --> 01:11:13.968
A person's heart
and a person's feelings...

01:11:14.003 --> 01:11:16.096
are very different than skates.

01:11:17.006 --> 01:11:18.268
Well, they're kind
of the same thing.

01:11:18.307 --> 01:11:20.275
If you aren't going
to use your heart...

01:11:20.309 --> 01:11:22.300
then what's the difference
if it gets broken?

01:11:22.344 --> 01:11:24.278
If you just keep it
to yourself...

01:11:24.313 --> 01:11:26.543
maybe it'll be like
my roller blades--

01:11:26.582 --> 01:11:28.550
when you do decide to try it...

01:11:28.584 --> 01:11:30.211
it won't be any good.

01:11:30.252 --> 01:11:31.719
You should take a chance.

01:11:31.754 --> 01:11:33.278
You got nothing to lose.

01:11:34.790 --> 01:11:36.621
A bit of truth in there
somewhere.

01:11:36.659 --> 01:11:38.126
I think so.

01:11:38.160 --> 01:11:39.855
Your heart
might still be broken...

01:11:39.895 --> 01:11:41.362
but it isn't gone.

01:11:41.397 --> 01:11:43.888
If it was gone,
you wouldn't be this nice.

01:11:44.933 --> 01:11:46.298
Thank you.

01:11:48.871 --> 01:11:50.099
Do you know that it's been...

01:11:51.874 --> 01:11:54.638
a couple of years
since I've talked to anybody?

01:11:54.677 --> 01:11:57.077
That's OK.
You're really good at it.

01:11:57.112 --> 01:11:58.238
You're not boring.

01:11:58.280 --> 01:12:00.077
You don't mumble or spit
when you talk.

01:12:00.115 --> 01:12:02.242
You should do it more often.

01:12:02.284 --> 01:12:03.581
You just have to wear
an outfit...

01:12:03.619 --> 01:12:05.211
that doesn't have
pigeon poop on it.

01:12:05.254 --> 01:12:07.245
[Woman laughs]

01:12:08.257 --> 01:12:09.724
Oh, I have been working
very hard...

01:12:09.758 --> 01:12:12.249
at keeping people away,
haven't l?

01:12:12.294 --> 01:12:15.024
I always think I'll have
a lot of fun if I'm alone...

01:12:15.064 --> 01:12:17.464
but being alone isn't much fun.

01:12:17.533 --> 01:12:20.229
I don't care how much
people bug me sometimes...

01:12:20.302 --> 01:12:23.328
I'd rather be with somebody
than by myself.

01:12:24.340 --> 01:12:25.830
So what are you doing
running around the streets...

01:12:25.908 --> 01:12:27.341
on Christmas Eve alone?

01:12:27.376 --> 01:12:29.344
Did you get into trouble?

01:12:29.378 --> 01:12:31.437
Yeah.

01:12:31.480 --> 01:12:33.004
WOMAN:
You've done something wrong?

01:12:33.048 --> 01:12:34.572
A lot of things.

01:12:36.985 --> 01:12:40.648
Did you know that a good deed
erases a bad deed?

01:12:40.689 --> 01:12:42.122
It's getting pretty late.

01:12:42.157 --> 01:12:44.182
I don't know
if I'll have enough time...

01:12:44.226 --> 01:12:46.888
to erase
all the bad deeds I did.

01:12:46.929 --> 01:12:48.726
Well, it's Christmas Eve.

01:12:48.764 --> 01:12:50.527
Good deeds
count for extra tonight.

01:12:50.599 --> 01:12:53.591
-They do?
-Of course they do.

01:12:53.669 --> 01:12:55.899
So you must think
of the most important thing...

01:12:55.938 --> 01:12:57.462
that you can do for others...

01:12:57.539 --> 01:12:59.166
and go and do it.

01:12:59.975 --> 01:13:02.170
Just follow the star
in your own heart.

01:13:03.779 --> 01:13:05.269
OK.

01:13:06.281 --> 01:13:07.748
It's getting pretty late.

01:13:07.783 --> 01:13:09.273
I better get going.

01:13:16.458 --> 01:13:19.757
If I don't see you again,
I hope everything turns out OK.

01:13:19.795 --> 01:13:21.126
Thank you.

01:13:22.331 --> 01:13:23.889
Say good-bye to your birds
for me.

01:13:23.966 --> 01:13:25.092
Oh, I will.

01:13:33.809 --> 01:13:34.935
Merry Christmas.

01:13:34.977 --> 01:13:36.376
Merry Christmas.

01:13:36.412 --> 01:13:39.870
If you need somebody to trust,
it can be me.

01:13:39.915 --> 01:13:42.247
I won't forget to remember you.

01:13:43.285 --> 01:13:45.253
Don't make promises
you can't keep.

01:14:01.069 --> 01:14:07.736
CHlLDREN SlNGlNG: Distant stars
at home up in the heavens

01:14:07.776 --> 01:14:11.234
Wonder what they see

01:14:11.280 --> 01:14:14.738
Are they watching me?

01:14:14.783 --> 01:14:17.752
Christmas star

01:14:17.786 --> 01:14:22.086
You watch the world so wisely

01:14:22.124 --> 01:14:26.060
At my journey's end

01:14:26.094 --> 01:14:29.154
Will you be my true friend?

01:14:29.231 --> 01:14:32.997
Starlight, shine bright

01:14:33.068 --> 01:14:37.004
See me through the dark night

01:14:37.072 --> 01:14:40.838
Light my pathway

01:14:40.876 --> 01:14:44.368
Guide me home for Christmas

01:14:44.413 --> 01:14:46.711
DUNCAN: All the money
in the cash register...

01:14:46.748 --> 01:14:50.411
Mr. Duncan is going to donate
to the Children's Hospital.

01:14:51.019 --> 01:14:54.682
MARV: At midnight tonight, we're
hitting Duncan's Toy Chest.

01:14:54.723 --> 01:14:56.714
You can mess
with a lot of things...

01:14:56.758 --> 01:14:59.727
but you can't mess with kids
on Christmas.

01:17:20.268 --> 01:17:21.360
CONClERGE:
We'd like to offer you...

01:17:21.436 --> 01:17:23.529
a complimentary suite
while you're here.

01:17:24.272 --> 01:17:26.740
It's a penthouse
with a view of the park.

01:17:26.775 --> 01:17:27.901
I think
you'll find it satisfactory.

01:17:27.943 --> 01:17:31.470
It was recently vacated by
the Countess of Worcestershire.

01:17:31.513 --> 01:17:34.846
What kind of hotel allows
a child to check in alone?

01:17:34.883 --> 01:17:37.545
The boy had a very
convincing story.

01:17:37.586 --> 01:17:39.986
What kind of idiots
are working here?

01:17:40.656 --> 01:17:43.489
The finest in New York.

01:17:43.525 --> 01:17:45.891
PETER: When you discovered
the credit card was stolen--

01:17:45.927 --> 01:17:48.020
I made the discovery.

01:17:48.063 --> 01:17:49.587
Why did you let him leave?

01:17:50.599 --> 01:17:52.590
When we attempted
to confront him, he ran.

01:17:52.668 --> 01:17:53.828
You scared him away.

01:17:53.902 --> 01:17:56.029
KATE: It's Christmas Eve,
and because of you...

01:17:56.104 --> 01:17:58.572
our child is lost in one of
the biggest cities in the world.

01:18:02.411 --> 01:18:04.936
Could you take our family
and our luggage up to the room?

01:18:04.980 --> 01:18:06.379
Yes, sir.

01:18:06.415 --> 01:18:07.814
Run along, Cedric.

01:18:07.849 --> 01:18:09.544
I'm going down
to the police station...

01:18:09.584 --> 01:18:11.711
and make sure
they're trying to find Kevin.

01:18:11.753 --> 01:18:13.550
I want you to stay
with the kids.

01:18:13.588 --> 01:18:16.079
-No. I'm going to look for him.
-What?

01:18:16.124 --> 01:18:17.557
With all due respect, madam...

01:18:17.592 --> 01:18:20.390
your son is lost in one of
the biggest cities in the world.

01:18:21.530 --> 01:18:23.498
Could you stay out of this,
please?

01:18:23.565 --> 01:18:25.123
As you wish.

01:18:25.200 --> 01:18:27.532
Thank you. I don't think
it's a good idea...

01:18:27.569 --> 01:18:30.436
for you to run around
New York City all by yourself.

01:18:30.472 --> 01:18:32.337
If our son can do it,
I can do it.

01:18:32.374 --> 01:18:33.671
Peter, I'll be fine.

01:18:33.709 --> 01:18:34.835
The way I'm feeling...

01:18:34.876 --> 01:18:36.867
no mugger or murderer
would dare mess with me.

01:18:38.346 --> 01:18:40.610
CONClERGE: Madam, there are
hundreds of parasites...

01:18:40.649 --> 01:18:41.980
armed to the teeth--

01:18:44.319 --> 01:18:46.810
Do bundle up.
It's awfully cold outside.

01:18:52.728 --> 01:18:54.719
[Clock chiming]

01:19:21.690 --> 01:19:24.090
Marv, Marv, come on. Let's go.

01:19:45.680 --> 01:19:47.113
Marv...

01:19:47.149 --> 01:19:48.309
crowbars up.

01:19:54.222 --> 01:19:55.985
Merry Christmas, Harry.

01:20:00.796 --> 01:20:03.287
Happy Hanukkah, Marv.

01:20:12.674 --> 01:20:15.768
MARV: This is more money
than I can even count.

01:20:15.811 --> 01:20:18.041
HARRY: Makes you wonder
why we spent so much time...

01:20:18.079 --> 01:20:19.205
robbing private homes.

01:20:19.247 --> 01:20:20.805
MARV: Ha ha!

01:20:33.829 --> 01:20:37.060
MARV: The amazing thing is,
we're fugitives from the law...

01:20:37.132 --> 01:20:39.498
we're up to our elbows
in cash...

01:20:39.534 --> 01:20:41.126
and nobody even knows about it.

01:20:45.440 --> 01:20:46.907
He's back!

01:20:48.276 --> 01:20:49.743
He took our picture!

01:20:49.778 --> 01:20:51.336
How did my hair look?

01:20:57.319 --> 01:20:58.809
KEVlN: This is it.

01:20:58.854 --> 01:21:00.344
No turning back.

01:21:01.356 --> 01:21:03.187
Another Christmas
in the trenches.

01:21:05.126 --> 01:21:08.857
No!

01:21:10.332 --> 01:21:12.323
[Alarm bell ringing]

01:21:12.400 --> 01:21:13.765
Wow.

01:21:13.802 --> 01:21:15.269
HARRY: That's it. Get the money!

01:21:15.303 --> 01:21:16.770
I'll kill him!

01:21:16.805 --> 01:21:18.705
That little friggin'
son of a dirty...

01:21:26.414 --> 01:21:28.177
-I'm coming, Harry!
-Marv!

01:21:28.717 --> 01:21:34.656
HARRY: Aah!

01:21:37.359 --> 01:21:38.621
Harry?

01:21:38.660 --> 01:21:40.855
Uhhh...

01:21:40.896 --> 01:21:42.124
Harry!

01:21:43.265 --> 01:21:44.357
That was incredible!

01:21:44.432 --> 01:21:46.900
[Mutters]

01:21:48.403 --> 01:21:50.268
I twisted my ankle
on that board there.

01:21:50.305 --> 01:21:53.399
-Where is he?
-Hey, guys, smile!

01:21:55.744 --> 01:21:57.371
HARRY: Come on. Come on!

01:21:57.412 --> 01:21:58.538
Help me.

01:21:58.580 --> 01:21:59.877
MARV: I got you.

01:21:59.915 --> 01:22:01.075
I got you.

01:22:27.542 --> 01:22:29.032
Taxi!

01:22:35.250 --> 01:22:36.410
Times Square.

01:22:58.273 --> 01:22:59.638
MARV: Where'd he go?

01:23:01.910 --> 01:23:03.901
KEVlN:
I'm up here! Come and get me!

01:23:05.447 --> 01:23:06.846
Let's kill!

01:23:06.881 --> 01:23:08.576
Hold on, pea-brain.

01:23:08.616 --> 01:23:09.844
We got busted last time...

01:23:09.884 --> 01:23:12.318
because we underestimated
that little bundle of misery.

01:23:12.354 --> 01:23:14.049
This ain't like the last time.

01:23:14.089 --> 01:23:16.319
This ain't his house.
The kid's running scared.

01:23:16.391 --> 01:23:18.052
He ain't got a plan.

01:23:19.260 --> 01:23:20.989
May I do the thinking, please?

01:23:22.731 --> 01:23:23.891
Thank you.

01:23:26.334 --> 01:23:27.460
Sonny!

01:23:27.502 --> 01:23:28.969
Yes?

01:23:29.004 --> 01:23:31.472
HARRY: Nothing would thrill me
more greatly...

01:23:31.506 --> 01:23:32.973
than to shoot you.

01:23:33.008 --> 01:23:34.475
Knocking off a youngster...

01:23:34.509 --> 01:23:37.342
ain't going to mean
all that much to me, understand?

01:23:37.379 --> 01:23:38.505
KEVlN: Mm-hmm.

01:23:38.546 --> 01:23:42.107
But since we're in a hurry,
I'll make a deal with you.

01:23:42.150 --> 01:23:44.311
You throw down your camera...

01:23:44.352 --> 01:23:46.820
and we won't hurt you.

01:23:46.855 --> 01:23:49.619
You'll never hear from us again.

01:23:49.691 --> 01:23:51.158
OK?

01:23:51.192 --> 01:23:52.557
You promise?

01:23:53.294 --> 01:23:56.821
I cross my heart
and hope to die.

01:23:56.898 --> 01:23:58.729
OK.

01:24:04.572 --> 01:24:07.234
OK, kid, give it to me.

01:24:14.182 --> 01:24:16.082
MARV: Ohh...

01:24:16.117 --> 01:24:17.311
Direct hit!

01:24:23.458 --> 01:24:25.449
How many fingers
am I holding up, Marv?

01:24:27.395 --> 01:24:28.521
Eight?

01:24:32.667 --> 01:24:34.931
OK, kid.
You want to throw bricks?

01:24:34.969 --> 01:24:36.527
Go ahead!
Throw another one!

01:24:42.243 --> 01:24:44.108
If you can't do any better
than that, kid...

01:24:44.145 --> 01:24:45.669
you're gonna lose!

01:24:47.015 --> 01:24:48.778
Harry...

01:24:48.817 --> 01:24:50.250
no.

01:24:56.191 --> 01:24:57.715
You got any more?

01:25:00.862 --> 01:25:03.729
Come on, Marv. Get up.
He's out of bricks.

01:25:09.204 --> 01:25:10.603
Ha ba...

01:25:10.638 --> 01:25:13.505
-What?
-[Gibberish]

01:25:13.541 --> 01:25:15.771
-What?
-[Gibberish]

01:25:16.778 --> 01:25:18.006
HARRY: What?

01:25:21.116 --> 01:25:22.242
That did it!

01:25:22.283 --> 01:25:24.114
Nobody throws bricks at me
and gets away with it!

01:25:24.152 --> 01:25:25.585
Marv, get up.

01:25:25.620 --> 01:25:27.053
You go this way,
I'll go around back.

01:25:31.993 --> 01:25:33.119
Harry?

01:25:34.662 --> 01:25:36.129
Harry?

01:25:37.665 --> 01:25:39.428
Harry?

01:26:03.191 --> 01:26:04.317
Huh?

01:26:28.383 --> 01:26:29.577
[Clack]

01:26:29.617 --> 01:26:32.609
Yeow!

01:26:37.659 --> 01:26:40.127
[Muttering]

01:26:52.607 --> 01:26:53.869
Oh!

01:26:58.446 --> 01:27:00.812
[Muttering]

01:27:25.873 --> 01:27:26.999
Ohh!

01:27:32.680 --> 01:27:35.672
[Muttering]

01:28:05.747 --> 01:28:08.580
MARV:
Harry, I've reached the top!

01:28:09.951 --> 01:28:12.784
Whoa--Aah!

01:28:18.026 --> 01:28:20.859
[Vertebrae crackle]

01:28:23.765 --> 01:28:25.323
Ahh.

01:28:26.768 --> 01:28:28.759
[Muttering]

01:28:38.179 --> 01:28:39.669
Yaah!

01:28:56.197 --> 01:28:57.824
HARRY: Ha ha ha ha ha!

01:29:01.569 --> 01:29:03.662
You got to do better
than this, kid!

01:29:05.239 --> 01:29:06.831
Ha ha ha--

01:29:09.410 --> 01:29:10.536
Ohh...

01:29:10.578 --> 01:29:11.738
Uh!

01:29:26.928 --> 01:29:28.327
-[Crack]
-Aah!

01:29:28.363 --> 01:29:30.194
Wow.

01:29:30.231 --> 01:29:31.721
What a hole.

01:29:53.154 --> 01:29:54.644
Whoa! Whoa!

01:29:58.926 --> 01:30:00.052
Oh!

01:30:06.434 --> 01:30:08.265
Oh!

01:30:08.302 --> 01:30:11.669
Aah! Aah!

01:30:11.706 --> 01:30:12.866
Uh-oh.

01:30:16.911 --> 01:30:18.572
Oh!

01:30:18.613 --> 01:30:19.739
Little creep!

01:30:19.781 --> 01:30:21.339
[Muttering]

01:30:41.068 --> 01:30:42.228
Ah!

01:31:02.190 --> 01:31:05.318
Aah!

01:31:41.229 --> 01:31:43.026
Ohh!

01:31:43.064 --> 01:31:45.123
Ohh!

01:31:45.166 --> 01:31:47.157
[Screaming]

01:32:05.520 --> 01:32:06.680
Aah!

01:32:31.846 --> 01:32:33.279
Heh heh heh heh heh heh.

01:32:44.025 --> 01:32:45.117
Oh!

01:32:45.192 --> 01:32:48.025
Ah! Ah! Ah! He did it!

01:33:39.780 --> 01:33:41.179
Harry?

01:34:02.470 --> 01:34:03.664
I'm coming up!

01:34:09.810 --> 01:34:11.437
Uh-oh.

01:34:18.986 --> 01:34:20.920
I'm going to murderthat kid.

01:34:22.757 --> 01:34:23.883
Ah-choo!

01:34:39.006 --> 01:34:40.200
Yes!

01:34:47.348 --> 01:34:48.508
Whoa!

01:34:56.991 --> 01:34:58.117
Whoop.

01:35:01.228 --> 01:35:02.354
Oh!

01:35:10.404 --> 01:35:11.803
MARV: Hey!

01:35:11.839 --> 01:35:14.967
Don't you know a kid always wins
against two idiots?

01:35:15.009 --> 01:35:17.477
Harry!
He's in the living room!

01:35:17.511 --> 01:35:18.773
[Muttering]

01:35:18.813 --> 01:35:19.973
He went up the ladder!

01:35:29.390 --> 01:35:32.518
Aah!

01:35:34.862 --> 01:35:37.057
Ohh...

01:35:38.032 --> 01:35:39.932
I'm coming, Harry.

01:35:39.967 --> 01:35:41.594
I'm coming.

01:35:46.741 --> 01:35:48.265
Harry, Harry.

01:35:49.744 --> 01:35:51.712
Hey, you didn't lose any teeth.

01:35:51.746 --> 01:35:53.213
Come on.
He went to the second floor.

01:35:54.115 --> 01:35:55.241
KEVlN: Hey...

01:35:55.282 --> 01:35:56.806
why don't you guys
try the stairs?

01:35:57.518 --> 01:35:58.678
MARV: Right.

01:36:01.756 --> 01:36:03.348
HARRY:
Wait a minute. Wait a minute!

01:36:04.191 --> 01:36:05.488
Don't you remember
what happened last year?

01:36:06.494 --> 01:36:07.620
No.

01:36:07.661 --> 01:36:09.185
Watch this.

01:36:10.498 --> 01:36:12.193
Let's get him!

01:36:12.233 --> 01:36:14.531
[Makes sound of footsteps]

01:36:16.403 --> 01:36:20.635
Oh! He busted me
right in my mouth, Marv!

01:36:20.708 --> 01:36:22.073
That's one.

01:36:22.109 --> 01:36:23.940
MARV: Don't worry, Harry!

01:36:25.379 --> 01:36:26.846
I'll get him!

01:36:31.786 --> 01:36:33.117
Ow!

01:36:33.988 --> 01:36:35.717
Right in the schnozz!

01:36:36.957 --> 01:36:38.618
HARRY: That's two.

01:36:38.659 --> 01:36:39.819
Come on. Let's get him.

01:36:43.164 --> 01:36:44.631
MARV: Oops.

01:36:44.665 --> 01:36:47.429
-Aah!
-Aah!

01:36:51.705 --> 01:36:53.332
MARV: That's...

01:36:53.407 --> 01:36:54.704
three.

01:37:00.548 --> 01:37:01.879
HARRY: No.

01:37:01.916 --> 01:37:03.577
[Clang]

01:37:03.617 --> 01:37:05.608
MARV: That's four.

01:37:10.324 --> 01:37:11.655
MARV: Come on, Harry.

01:37:11.692 --> 01:37:13.489
HARRY:
Marv, are you sure this is safe?

01:37:13.527 --> 01:37:14.960
MARV: Oh, yeah.

01:37:14.995 --> 01:37:17.293
Yup. I worked all the kinks out.

01:37:17.331 --> 01:37:19.196
Solid as a rock.

01:37:33.113 --> 01:37:34.580
[Furniture collapsing]

01:37:36.050 --> 01:37:37.950
HARRY: Like a rock, huh, Marv?

01:37:37.985 --> 01:37:39.612
KEVlN: Hey, do you guys give up?

01:37:39.653 --> 01:37:41.120
Have you had enough pain?

01:37:41.155 --> 01:37:42.315
MARV: Never!

01:37:54.535 --> 01:37:57.026
HARRY: You better say every
prayer you ever heard before!

01:37:57.071 --> 01:38:00.063
MARV: I hope your parents got
you a tombstone for Christmas!

01:38:02.509 --> 01:38:03.635
Where'd he go?

01:38:04.411 --> 01:38:07.141
I'm up here,
and I'm really scared.

01:38:16.757 --> 01:38:17.917
HARRY: What's that sound?

01:38:28.202 --> 01:38:29.829
-Aah!
-Aah!

01:38:38.746 --> 01:38:41.044
MARV: That was the sound
of a tool chest...

01:38:41.081 --> 01:38:43.641
falling down the stairs.

01:38:43.684 --> 01:38:44.981
HARRY: Oh.

01:38:47.121 --> 01:38:48.247
[Crunch]

01:38:50.090 --> 01:38:51.250
Yes!

01:39:26.160 --> 01:39:27.320
MARV: Over there!

01:39:28.228 --> 01:39:30.423
HARRY: I don't care if I get
the chair. I'm killing that kid!

01:39:33.600 --> 01:39:35.659
HARRY: Surrender, kid!

01:39:35.703 --> 01:39:36.829
MARV: He vanished.

01:39:36.870 --> 01:39:38.804
KEVlN: I'm down here,
you big horse's ass!

01:39:42.643 --> 01:39:43.735
MARV: Whoa!

01:39:43.811 --> 01:39:45.540
Nice night for a neck injury!

01:39:47.081 --> 01:39:49.879
Suck brick, kid!

01:39:55.189 --> 01:39:56.679
HARRY: Come on, Marv.

01:39:56.724 --> 01:39:58.692
MARV: Oh, I don't know.

01:39:58.726 --> 01:40:00.489
HARRY: I said, come on.

01:40:02.162 --> 01:40:04.824
Come on, you big sissy.

01:40:04.865 --> 01:40:06.856
[Whimpering]

01:40:15.442 --> 01:40:17.410
[Sniffing]

01:40:18.579 --> 01:40:19.978
Harry?

01:40:20.014 --> 01:40:21.481
You wearing aftershave?

01:40:21.515 --> 01:40:23.506
HARRY: That's not aftershave.
That's kerosene.

01:40:24.318 --> 01:40:25.842
The rope is soaked in it.

01:40:26.954 --> 01:40:29.252
Why would anybody
soak a rope in kerosene?

01:40:33.894 --> 01:40:35.225
Merry Christmas.

01:40:36.430 --> 01:40:38.830
-Go up!
-Aah!

01:40:47.775 --> 01:40:48.901
Aah!

01:40:52.646 --> 01:40:54.204
HARRY: Ooch! Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

01:40:54.281 --> 01:40:56.306
Ouch! Aah! Ouch!

01:40:59.787 --> 01:41:01.482
MARV: Aah!

01:41:04.558 --> 01:41:12.021
-Aah!
-Aah!

01:41:12.066 --> 01:41:13.363
HARRY: Get off!

01:41:14.768 --> 01:41:16.827
-Aah!
-Aah!

01:41:37.858 --> 01:41:39.018
HARRY: Get the bag.

01:41:39.893 --> 01:41:42.487
Hello. The two guys who robbed
Duncan's Toy Chest...

01:41:42.529 --> 01:41:45.430
are at Central Park West
and 95th Street.

01:41:45.466 --> 01:41:46.592
Look for fireworks.

01:41:46.633 --> 01:41:47.964
Hurry. They got a gun.

01:41:54.708 --> 01:41:55.800
KEVlN: Hey, I'm down here.

01:41:55.876 --> 01:41:58.436
Better come and get me
before I call the cops.

01:42:02.549 --> 01:42:04.039
[Bus horn honks]

01:42:06.353 --> 01:42:07.684
Whoa!

01:42:13.794 --> 01:42:16.922
MARV:
My, how the tables have turned.

01:42:16.964 --> 01:42:18.659
HARRY:
How do you like the ice, kid?

01:42:19.700 --> 01:42:20.962
[Both laughing]

01:42:24.538 --> 01:42:26.699
HARRY: Let's go
for a little stroll in the park.

01:42:44.291 --> 01:42:45.553
HARRY: Give me that bag!

01:42:45.592 --> 01:42:46.718
Gimme it.

01:42:51.965 --> 01:42:54.297
These will look great
in the photo album.

01:42:55.269 --> 01:42:57.100
You may have won
the battle, little dude...

01:42:57.137 --> 01:42:58.968
but you lost the war.

01:42:59.706 --> 01:43:01.765
HARRY: You ought not have
messed with us, pal.

01:43:01.842 --> 01:43:03.241
We're dangerous.

01:43:09.283 --> 01:43:11.410
-Harry.
-Shut up.

01:43:15.789 --> 01:43:16.915
Harry...

01:43:16.957 --> 01:43:18.788
HARRY:
Shut up. I want to enjoy this.

01:43:19.793 --> 01:43:21.522
MARV: Something's wrong.

01:43:22.429 --> 01:43:23.760
Let's get out of here.

01:43:23.797 --> 01:43:24.957
Shut up, I said!

01:43:27.100 --> 01:43:29.227
HARRY: I never made it
to the sixth grade, kid...

01:43:29.269 --> 01:43:32.067
and it doesn't look like
you're going to, either.

01:43:33.273 --> 01:43:34.740
WOMAN: Let him go!

01:43:35.776 --> 01:43:37.334
Kevin, run!

01:43:39.279 --> 01:43:41.509
Shoot her! Shoot her!

01:43:42.115 --> 01:43:43.241
Shoot her!

01:43:43.283 --> 01:43:44.750
I'm trying to shoot her!

01:43:55.128 --> 01:43:59.155
-Aah!
-Aah!

01:44:10.844 --> 01:44:12.573
[Harry muttering]

01:44:15.515 --> 01:44:22.751
Aah!

01:44:24.758 --> 01:44:25.986
Bye! Thanks!

01:44:46.280 --> 01:44:48.248
[Siren]

01:44:52.386 --> 01:44:54.718
OFFlCER: Jeez, it looks like
the Fourth of July!

01:44:55.956 --> 01:44:58.015
We'll take the bridge.
You guys get the tunnel.

01:44:58.058 --> 01:44:59.548
Let's go. Come on!

01:45:02.195 --> 01:45:03.685
[Harry and Marv muttering]

01:45:07.301 --> 01:45:08.996
Oh, my God!

01:45:09.036 --> 01:45:10.367
[Gunshot]

01:45:19.646 --> 01:45:21.045
OFFlCER:
All right, you guys, let's go.

01:45:21.081 --> 01:45:23.015
SECOND OFFlCER:
Come on. On yourfeet.

01:45:23.050 --> 01:45:24.210
HARRY: Take it easy.

01:45:28.021 --> 01:45:30.251
OFFlCER: You guys
should've started earlier.

01:45:30.290 --> 01:45:32.520
The prisoners
have already exchanged gifts.

01:45:32.559 --> 01:45:34.527
MARV: We missed the presents?

01:45:34.561 --> 01:45:35.926
He made us hide out
in a store...

01:45:35.962 --> 01:45:38.590
so we could steal
the charity money.

01:45:38.632 --> 01:45:40.429
-Shut up, Marv!
-Aah!

01:45:41.435 --> 01:45:43.801
HARRY: You got the right
to remain silent, you know.

01:45:44.705 --> 01:45:45.933
He's a little cranky.

01:45:46.006 --> 01:45:47.701
We just broke out of prison
a few days ago.

01:45:47.774 --> 01:45:50.436
Shut up, Marv! Jeez!

01:45:50.510 --> 01:45:52.774
-Get them out of here.
-Let's go.

01:45:52.813 --> 01:45:54.508
MARV: Remember,
if this makes the papers...

01:45:54.548 --> 01:45:56.106
we're no longer the Wet Bandits.

01:45:56.149 --> 01:45:57.776
We're the Sticky Bandits!

01:45:57.818 --> 01:46:00.412
Ow! That's Sticky!
That's "S"...

01:46:00.454 --> 01:46:01.580
HARRY: Shut it!

01:46:01.621 --> 01:46:02.952
MARV: "T," uh...

01:46:02.989 --> 01:46:05.116
-"l."
-"l."

01:46:17.003 --> 01:46:18.493
OFFlCER:
Mr. Duncan, it's all over.

01:46:18.538 --> 01:46:20.699
We apprehended the thieves,
and we recovered your money.

01:46:20.774 --> 01:46:22.036
DUNCAN: Good.
I want to get that money...

01:46:22.109 --> 01:46:24.509
over to the Children's Hospital.

01:46:24.544 --> 01:46:26.034
OFFlCER:
I'll handle it personally.

01:46:26.113 --> 01:46:27.580
DUNCAN: Thank you very much.

01:46:27.614 --> 01:46:29.377
INSPECTOR:
Excuse me, Mr. Duncan.

01:46:29.416 --> 01:46:30.849
I found this note.

01:46:30.884 --> 01:46:32.818
Looks like a kid
broke your window.

01:46:49.736 --> 01:46:52.398
Turtledoves.

01:46:52.472 --> 01:46:53.632
Ohh.

01:47:01.081 --> 01:47:02.776
KATE: Oh, excuse me.
I'm looking for my son.

01:47:02.816 --> 01:47:04.113
He's this boy right here.

01:47:06.586 --> 01:47:07.848
Excuse me. Please help me.

01:47:07.921 --> 01:47:09.047
This boy right here,
have you seen him?

01:47:09.122 --> 01:47:10.919
This one. Please?

01:47:19.533 --> 01:47:21.000
I'm looking for my son.

01:47:21.034 --> 01:47:23.002
He's been missing
for two days.

01:47:23.036 --> 01:47:24.503
OFFlCER:
Have you filed a report?

01:47:24.538 --> 01:47:26.005
KATE: Yes, of course we have.

01:47:28.108 --> 01:47:29.473
Then trust us.

01:47:29.509 --> 01:47:30.669
We'll handle it.

01:47:32.579 --> 01:47:33.739
Oh.

01:47:36.049 --> 01:47:37.209
But I'm his mother.

01:47:38.919 --> 01:47:40.011
I realize that, ma'am...

01:47:40.086 --> 01:47:41.576
but you're looking
for a needle in a haystack.

01:47:42.756 --> 01:47:44.246
Do you have kids?

01:47:45.325 --> 01:47:46.451
Yes, ma'am.

01:47:46.493 --> 01:47:48.461
And what would you do
if one of them was missing?

01:47:50.464 --> 01:47:53.558
I'd probably be doing
the same thing you're doing.

01:47:54.568 --> 01:47:55.728
Thank you.

01:47:58.338 --> 01:48:00.465
Look, put yourself
in your kid's shoes.

01:48:00.507 --> 01:48:02.873
Where would you go?
What would you do?

01:48:02.909 --> 01:48:06.003
Me? I'd probably be lying dead
in a gutter somewhere.

01:48:07.514 --> 01:48:08.947
Oh, but not Kevin.

01:48:08.982 --> 01:48:12.748
No. Kevin is so much stronger
and braver than I am.

01:48:14.154 --> 01:48:16.486
I know Kevin's fine.
I'm sure he is.

01:48:16.523 --> 01:48:18.320
Fine.

01:48:18.358 --> 01:48:20.519
But he's still all by himself
in a big city...

01:48:21.895 --> 01:48:23.726
and he doesn't deserve that.

01:48:23.763 --> 01:48:26.391
He deserves to be at home
with his own family...

01:48:26.433 --> 01:48:28.094
around his Christmas tree.

01:48:31.771 --> 01:48:33.102
Oh, dear God.

01:48:34.374 --> 01:48:35.602
I know where he is.

01:48:36.576 --> 01:48:38.100
I need to get
to Rockefeller Center.

01:48:39.045 --> 01:48:40.171
Hop in.

01:48:40.213 --> 01:48:41.737
Thank you.

01:48:45.986 --> 01:48:48.045
KEVlN: I know I don't deserve
a Christmas...

01:48:48.121 --> 01:48:50.089
even if I did do a good deed.

01:48:51.124 --> 01:48:52.682
I don't want any presents.

01:48:52.759 --> 01:48:54.488
Instead, I want to take back...

01:48:54.528 --> 01:48:57.190
every mean thing
I ever said to my family....

01:48:57.230 --> 01:48:59.460
even if they don't take back
the things they said.

01:48:59.499 --> 01:49:01.899
I don't care.
I'll love all of them...

01:49:02.903 --> 01:49:04.530
including Buzz.

01:49:04.571 --> 01:49:08.337
If I can only see one,
can I see my mother?

01:49:08.375 --> 01:49:11.902
I'll never want another thing
as long as I live.

01:49:11.945 --> 01:49:13.412
I just want my mother.

01:49:13.446 --> 01:49:15.346
I know I won't see her
tonight...

01:49:15.382 --> 01:49:17.907
but promise me
I can see her again...

01:49:17.951 --> 01:49:19.942
sometime, anytime.

01:49:19.986 --> 01:49:23.922
Even if it's just once and only
for a couple of minutes.

01:49:23.990 --> 01:49:26.288
I just need to tell her
I'm sorry.

01:49:34.367 --> 01:49:35.527
Kevin?

01:49:42.342 --> 01:49:43.502
Mom?

01:49:46.212 --> 01:49:47.907
Wow. That worked fast.

01:49:58.558 --> 01:49:59.855
KATE: Oh, Kevin.

01:50:01.728 --> 01:50:03.628
Mom, I'm sorry.

01:50:05.165 --> 01:50:06.655
I'm sorry, too.

01:50:19.546 --> 01:50:21.207
KEVlN: Merry Christmas, Mom.

01:50:23.550 --> 01:50:25.677
KATE:
Merry Christmas, sweetheart.

01:50:26.720 --> 01:50:28.085
Thank you.

01:50:29.155 --> 01:50:30.383
Let's go.

01:50:31.391 --> 01:50:32.858
KEVlN:
How'd you know I was here?

01:50:32.926 --> 01:50:34.154
KATE: I know you
and Christmas trees...

01:50:34.194 --> 01:50:35.786
and this is the biggest around.

01:50:35.829 --> 01:50:37.023
KEVlN: Where's everybody else?

01:50:37.063 --> 01:50:38.189
KATE: They're at the hotel.

01:50:38.231 --> 01:50:39.892
They didn't like
the palm trees, either.

01:51:02.455 --> 01:51:03.888
[Snoring]

01:51:24.044 --> 01:51:26.774
Holy smokes! It's morning!

01:51:28.148 --> 01:51:29.945
It's Christmas morning, man.

01:51:31.384 --> 01:51:33.682
Fuller, don't get your hopes up.

01:51:33.753 --> 01:51:35.243
FULLER: Huh?

01:51:35.321 --> 01:51:37.255
I don't think
Santa Claus visits hotels.

01:51:37.290 --> 01:51:39.758
Are you nuts? He's omnipresent.

01:51:39.826 --> 01:51:41.521
He goes everywhere.

01:51:43.163 --> 01:51:45.063
Hey, guys, wake up!
It's Christmas!

01:51:49.736 --> 01:51:50.862
Mom, Dad, it's Christmas!

01:51:50.904 --> 01:51:52.064
FRANK: What?!

01:51:55.675 --> 01:51:56.937
GlRL: What on earth?

01:51:56.976 --> 01:51:58.466
JEFF: Come on. I wanna find out.

01:52:03.983 --> 01:52:05.644
ROD: Oh, wow.

01:52:05.719 --> 01:52:07.687
JEFF:
Where did it all come from?

01:52:07.721 --> 01:52:09.780
KEVlN:
Mom! Dad! You got to see this!

01:52:14.394 --> 01:52:16.294
-Gosh.
-Peter!

01:52:16.329 --> 01:52:17.694
BUZZ: Are you sure
we're in the right room?

01:52:19.032 --> 01:52:21.227
-Look at all this stuff!
-Yeah!

01:52:21.267 --> 01:52:23.360
-Oh, wow!
-Look!

01:52:24.037 --> 01:52:25.698
FRANK: Don't open any of mine.
I mean it.

01:52:25.739 --> 01:52:27.206
Who's Mr. Duncan?

01:52:27.240 --> 01:52:29.299
KATE: Duncan? I don't know.

01:52:29.342 --> 01:52:30.639
All right.
Everyone just calm down.

01:52:30.677 --> 01:52:33.373
Calm down. Hey, hey!

01:52:33.413 --> 01:52:35.438
All right. Now...

01:52:35.482 --> 01:52:40.215
if Kevin hadn't screwed up
in the first place again...

01:52:40.286 --> 01:52:43.847
then we wouldn't be in this most
perfect and huge hotel room...

01:52:43.923 --> 01:52:45.857
with a truckload
of all this free stuff...

01:52:45.892 --> 01:52:47.519
so...

01:52:47.560 --> 01:52:48.686
I think it only fair...

01:52:48.728 --> 01:52:51.356
that Kevin get to open up
the first present.

01:52:51.998 --> 01:52:53.124
Then I'll go...

01:52:53.166 --> 01:52:54.793
and the rest of you, and so on.

01:52:59.272 --> 01:53:01.900
Merry Christmas, Kev.

01:53:01.941 --> 01:53:03.704
Merry Christmas, Buzz.

01:53:06.379 --> 01:53:07.505
PETER: Merry Christmas, Kevin.

01:53:07.547 --> 01:53:09.242
FRANK: OK, Kevin!

01:53:09.282 --> 01:53:11.512
All right! Merry Christmas!

01:53:13.586 --> 01:53:15.611
Enough of this gooey sh--

01:53:15.688 --> 01:53:17.349
show...of emotion.

01:53:17.423 --> 01:53:18.515
Everyone, let's dig in!

01:53:18.591 --> 01:53:21.754
-All right!
-Everybody, wait.

01:53:21.795 --> 01:53:23.353
LESLlE: Save the paper.
We can use it next year.

01:53:23.396 --> 01:53:25.455
Give me the bows.

01:54:01.034 --> 01:54:02.661
Merry Christmas.

01:54:05.138 --> 01:54:06.571
Kevin!

